{
 "schema": "v3lum.web_fingerprint.waf/1",
 "source": "https://github.com/EnableSecurity/wafw00f (wafw00f/plugins/*.py, is_waf header/cookie checks on the NORMAL response only)",
 "commit": "69fbe3956bba47a172cf87e40e9037535d32a130 2026-04-19T18:17:41+05:30",
 "licence": "BSD-3-Clause",
 "notice": "Copyright (c) 2009-2026, WAFW00F Developers. All rights reserved. Redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without modification, are permitted provided that the conditions of the BSD-3-Clause licence are met (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).",
 "semantics": "A signature matches when ANY rule matches; a rule is an expression tree of all/any over leaves. header leaf: re.search(regex, value, re.I) on the named response header (case-insensitive name); cookie leaf: re.search on each Set-Cookie header value separately. Rules that need matchContent/matchStatus/matchReason or attack=True (attack-payload probes) were dropped, never ported (FC6). kind: waf (a WAF product) or cdn_or_proxy (a proxy/CDN/load balancer front end, never reported as \"protected by WAF\"). Fixes: Shieldon header name [xx]-[pp]rotected-[bb]y (a dead regex in wafw00f) read as x-protected-by. Leading/trailing (.*)? and .* were removed from the regexes (equivalent under re.search, linear time on 8 KB header values: P072 cond 5 time budget). Two optional prefixes that made a regex quadratic were dropped: '(\\\\w+\\\\.)?airee\\\\.cloud' -> 'airee\\\\.cloud' and the CloudFront Via regex -> ' [\\\\w-]+\\\\.cloudfront\\\\.net \\\\(Cloudfront\\\\)'.",
 "stats": {
  "plugins": 172,
  "unsupported": [],
  "rules_total": 416,
  "rules_passive": 170,
  "plugins_with_passive": 101,
  "bad_regex": []
 },
